From a959e59c64b55dd17a974dda4c4b71dff520af3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Farris <briandavidfarris@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 06:38:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Drain the sd-bus queue in the check pass

sd-bus queues messages internally, and a synchronous sd_bus_call_method()
queues every unrelated message it reads while waiting for its own reply.
The fd is not readable while messages sit in that queue, so poll() never
wakes the event loop, and a Session.Lock signal received during the
SetIdleHint call is not dispatched until later bus traffic arrives.

Drain the queue in the wl_event_source_check() pass, as display_event()
already does for the Wayland display.

Fixes: https://github.com/swaywm/swayidle/issues/204
---
 main.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index c6bdab6f..cd5375b4 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -412,6 +412,9 @@ static int dbus_event(int fd, uint32_t mask, void *data) {
 		sd_bus_flush(bus);
 	}
 	if (mask == 0) {
+		while ((count = sd_bus_process(bus, NULL)) > 0) {
+			// Keep going until the queue is empty.
+		}
 		sd_bus_flush(bus);
 	}
 
